# This repository builds a Linux disk image. Every file in it is a shell script,
# a config fragment, or a systemd unit that gets executed on Debian — including
# from a Windows checkout via WSL or Docker.
#
# Git for Windows ships with core.autocrlf=true in its SYSTEM config, which
# rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout. A shell script with CRLF line endings fails at
# runtime with "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M", which does not name line endings
# as the cause. Pin LF here so the setting cannot reach this repository.
* text=auto eol=lf
